WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.291 --> 00:00:30.875
At the beginning of Chapter 13,

2
00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:34.791
Lord Krishna introduced the kshetra
and the kshetrajna.

3
00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:38.125
Now, from verses 13.8 through 13.12,

4
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:40.333
He explains the process of jnana, knowledge,

5
00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:43.916
that frees a person from the bondage of
the material world

6
00:00:43.916 --> 00:00:47.875
and ultimately leads to the realisation
of the supreme truth.

7
00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:49.500
This process is made up

8
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.541
of twenty qualities and practices

9
00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:55.000
that cultivate virtues and disciplines,

10
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.666
leading toward spiritual growth.

11
00:00:57.666 --> 00:00:59.583
These qualities form the foundation

12
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:01.375
for understanding the distinction

13
00:01:01.375 --> 00:01:05.708
between the body and the soul,

14
00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:06.791
and help in the direct

15
00:01:06.791 --> 00:01:10.541
experience of the supreme truth.

16
00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:12.291
These twenty qualities serve

17
00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:14.666
two purposes:

18
00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:18.291
For devotees, they develop naturally

19
00:01:18.291 --> 00:01:22.208
as fruits of pure devotion.

20
00:01:22.208 --> 00:01:25.208
As one advances in devotion,

21
00:01:25.208 --> 00:01:29.583
devotion itself bestows these qualities.

22
00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:32.416
For those on the path of knowledge,

23
00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:34.041
these qualities

24
00:01:34.041 --> 00:01:37.166
form a systematic discipline

25
00:01:37.166 --> 00:01:39.333
for purifying the mind

26
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:42.958
and preparing for self-realisation.

27
00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:50.916
Amaanitvam, humility.

28
00:01:50.916 --> 00:01:54.166
Humility means not expecting respect

29
00:01:54.166 --> 00:01:57.458
from others for oneself.

30
00:01:57.458 --> 00:02:00.958
This feeling comes when we understand

31
00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:03.958
that all our talents and successes

32
00:02:03.958 --> 00:02:06.375
are gifts of the Supreme.

33
00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:09.375
A humble person does not crave praise

34
00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:13.333
and remains indifferent to worldly fame.

35
00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.000
True humility is accepting that

36
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.291
you are only an instrument of God,

37
00:02:19.291 --> 00:02:21.833
your purpose is to serve,

38
00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:24.250
not to gain glory.

39
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.666
Adambhitvam, the absence of pride.

40
00:02:28.666 --> 00:02:31.000
This means staying away

41
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.291
from pretence and false display.

42
00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:38.333
It means not trying to appear

43
00:02:38.333 --> 00:02:41.833
or be what you are not.

44
00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:43.625
Where humility protects you

45
00:02:43.625 --> 00:02:47.583
from arrogance despite real achievement,

46
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:49.750
the absence of pride stops you

47
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.791
from false pride

48
00:02:51.791 --> 00:02:54.500
in what you do not have.

49
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.583
Such a person neither deceives

50
00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:58.458
nor chases appearances,

51
00:02:58.458 --> 00:03:03.041
their conduct is genuine and natural.

52
00:03:03.041 --> 00:03:05.791
Ahimsa, non-violence.

53
00:03:05.791 --> 00:03:08.833
This means causing no harm to any being

54
00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:12.833
through thought, word, or action.

55
00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:15.875
True ahimsa is connected not only

56
00:03:15.875 --> 00:03:18.416
to physical harm but also to the feeling

57
00:03:18.416 --> 00:03:22.416
of avoiding mental and emotional pain.

58
00:03:22.416 --> 00:03:24.625
Lord Krishna emphasises

59
00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:27.666
that real ahimsa includes giving others

60
00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:30.875
spiritual knowledge and freeing them

61
00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:32.333
from suffering.

62
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:35.291
Obstructing someone's spiritual progress

63
00:03:35.291 --> 00:03:38.791
is itself a great form of violence.

64
00:03:38.791 --> 00:03:42.541
Kshanti, forbearance.

65
00:03:42.541 --> 00:03:44.541
This means patiently enduring

66
00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:47.541
insult, hardship, and provocation

67
00:03:47.541 --> 00:03:52.458
without seeking revenge.

68
00:03:52.458 --> 00:03:54.291
It is the ability to maintain

69
00:03:54.291 --> 00:03:57.250
composure despite challenges

70
00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.875
and keep full focus on spiritual goals.

71
00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:03.125
Even when facing opposition,

72
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:05.333
the one who practises forbearance

73
00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:07.958
remains unshaken.

74
00:04:07.958 --> 00:04:11.500
They walk the path of dharma
with steadfastness,

75
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.458
as Prahlad Maharaj

76
00:04:13.458 --> 00:04:15.208
patiently endured

77
00:04:15.208 --> 00:04:18.541
his father's tortures.

78
00:04:18.541 --> 00:04:19.583
Arjavam,

79
00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:24.500
straightforwardness or sincerity.

80
00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.708
This means dealing

81
00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:27.333
with others truthfully

82
00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.250
and openly.

83
00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.875
It includes avoiding deception,

84
00:04:30.875 --> 00:04:33.958
guile, and manipulation.

85
00:04:33.958 --> 00:04:36.125
A straightforward person speaks from the heart

86
00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:38.958
without any hidden intention

87
00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:43.958
and maintains purity in thought, word, and deed.

88
00:04:43.958 --> 00:04:46.416
Acharyopasanam,

89
00:04:46.416 --> 00:04:49.958
taking shelter of a true spiritual teacher.

90
00:04:49.958 --> 00:04:52.958
Approaching a true spiritual teacher
with humility

91
00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:55.916
and a genuine desire to learn

92
00:04:55.916 --> 00:04:59.000
is essential for gaining knowledge.

93
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.791
Serving the spiritual teacher sincerely

94
00:05:01.791 --> 00:05:05.041
and following their instructions with faith

95
00:05:05.041 --> 00:05:08.208
opens the door to spiritual progress.

96
00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:09.041
The blessing

97
00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:10.666
of a true teacher

98
00:05:10.666 --> 00:05:12.875
can accelerate spiritual growth

99
00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:17.583
and make following the disciplines easier.

100
00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:20.833
Shaucham, purity.

101
00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.916
This means both outer

102
00:05:22.916 --> 00:05:27.250
and inner cleanliness.

103
00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:28.708
Outer purity:

104
00:05:28.708 --> 00:05:31.833
maintaining regular bathing and cleanliness.

105
00:05:31.833 --> 00:05:33.333
Inner purity:

106
00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.458
cleanliness of the mind through

107
00:05:35.458 --> 00:05:37.375
continuous remembrance of Lord Krishna,

108
00:05:37.375 --> 00:05:39.000
chanting His holy names,

109
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.916
and cultivating positive thoughts.

110
00:05:42.916 --> 00:05:45.375
True purity involves aligning

111
00:05:45.375 --> 00:05:47.000
and purifying consciousness

112
00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.041
with spiritual truth.

113
00:05:50.041 --> 00:05:54.833
Sthairyam, steadfastness or resolve.

114
00:05:54.833 --> 00:05:56.458
This means an unwavering

115
00:05:56.458 --> 00:05:58.875
commitment to the spiritual path

116
00:05:58.875 --> 00:06:01.416
despite challenges

117
00:06:01.416 --> 00:06:03.541
or distractions.

118
00:06:03.541 --> 00:06:05.250
It is the ability to remain firm

119
00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.250
in the pursuit of self-realisation

120
00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.291
without worrying about obstacles.

121
00:06:10.291 --> 00:06:11.375
The steadfast seeker

122
00:06:11.375 --> 00:06:14.333
is not unsettled by temporary difficulties

123
00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:18.708
but remains focused on the ultimate goal.

124
00:06:18.708 --> 00:06:22.916
Atmavinigrahah, self-control.

125
00:06:22.916 --> 00:06:25.125
This means keeping the mind

126
00:06:25.125 --> 00:06:26.833
and senses from engaging

127
00:06:26.833 --> 00:06:28.583
in activities

128
00:06:28.583 --> 00:06:32.791
that obstruct spiritual progress.

129
00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:33.625
The senses

130
00:06:33.625 --> 00:06:34.833
naturally

131
00:06:34.833 --> 00:06:36.833
crave satisfaction,

132
00:06:36.833 --> 00:06:37.666
but one who

133
00:06:37.666 --> 00:06:39.416
practises self-control

134
00:06:39.416 --> 00:06:42.541
disciplines these desires

135
00:06:42.541 --> 00:06:45.083
and accepts only what is necessary

136
00:06:45.083 --> 00:06:46.625
to maintain the body

137
00:06:46.625 --> 00:06:51.000
for the service of the Supreme.

138
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.375
Special emphasis is placed

139
00:06:53.375 --> 00:06:54.625
on control of the tongue,

140
00:06:54.625 --> 00:06:57.750
which craves both taste and speech.

141
00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.000
Here Lord Krishna

142
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.250
is explaining everything with simplicity.

143
00:07:07.041 --> 00:07:10.708
Do you wish to grow in life,

144
00:07:10.708 --> 00:07:12.791
not only in what

145
00:07:12.791 --> 00:07:16.833
you achieve,

146
00:07:16.833 --> 00:07:20.125
but in what you become?

147
00:07:20.125 --> 00:07:22.750
Then begin with humility

148
00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:27.916
and the absence of pride.

149
00:07:27.916 --> 00:07:29.250
These are not merely

150
00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:33.291
spiritual virtues,

151
00:07:33.291 --> 00:07:35.041
they are the foundation

152
00:07:35.041 --> 00:07:38.166
of personal growth.

153
00:07:38.166 --> 00:07:40.500
Humility does not mean

154
00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:44.875
putting yourself down.

155
00:07:44.875 --> 00:07:48.083
It means knowing

156
00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:52.708
that your talents, skills, and opportunities

157
00:07:52.708 --> 00:07:56.791
are not yours alone,

158
00:07:56.791 --> 00:07:59.958
they are blessings.

159
00:07:59.958 --> 00:08:02.625
When you stop chasing praise

160
00:08:02.625 --> 00:08:07.791
and recognition,

161
00:08:07.791 --> 00:08:12.291
you become free.

162
00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:14.375
You grow because

163
00:08:14.375 --> 00:08:17.708
you want to,

164
00:08:17.708 --> 00:08:21.750
not because others are watching.

165
00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.625
The absence of pride means

166
00:08:24.625 --> 00:08:27.541
not pretending to be more

167
00:08:27.541 --> 00:08:32.333
than you are.

168
00:08:32.333 --> 00:08:35.000
No false display,

169
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.583
no unnecessary image-building,

170
00:08:38.583 --> 00:08:40.708
only honesty with yourself

171
00:08:40.708 --> 00:08:44.541
and with others.

172
00:08:44.541 --> 00:08:45.583
When you are

173
00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:49.791
not trying to impress the world,

174
00:08:49.791 --> 00:08:52.541
life becomes lighter.

175
00:08:52.541 --> 00:08:56.125
When you hold both humility

176
00:08:56.125 --> 00:08:58.791
and truthfulness,

177
00:08:58.791 --> 00:09:02.041
learning becomes easier,

178
00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:04.000
others' responses

179
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:08.333
begin to help you, and relationships

180
00:09:08.333 --> 00:09:10.625
become more genuine.

181
00:09:10.625 --> 00:09:13.333
These qualities may not

182
00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:17.125
announce themselves loudly,

183
00:09:17.125 --> 00:09:18.916
but they

184
00:09:18.916 --> 00:09:24.125
quietly build a meaningful, steady,

185
00:09:24.125 --> 00:09:27.833
and joyful life.

186
00:09:32.666 --> 00:09:34.833
Do you know

187
00:09:34.833 --> 00:09:36.708
what truly holds

188
00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:39.541
a family together?

189
00:09:39.541 --> 00:09:41.416
It is not only love

190
00:09:41.416 --> 00:09:44.125
or shared routine,

191
00:09:44.125 --> 00:09:48.625
it is forbearance.

192
00:09:48.625 --> 00:09:52.500
In a family, everyone is different.

193
00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:55.666
Habits, thoughts,

194
00:09:55.666 --> 00:09:59.333
natures, and ways of expression,

195
00:09:59.333 --> 00:10:02.541
all differ.

196
00:10:02.541 --> 00:10:04.625
Without forbearance,

197
00:10:04.625 --> 00:10:06.541
even small matters

198
00:10:06.541 --> 00:10:10.000
can cause pain and distance.

199
00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:14.375
When you learn to listen with patience,

200
00:10:14.375 --> 00:10:17.166
when you stop reacting

201
00:10:17.166 --> 00:10:20.833
to every small irritation,

202
00:10:20.833 --> 00:10:25.500
you create space for mutual understanding.

203
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.125
Forbearance does not mean

204
00:10:28.125 --> 00:10:31.541
agreeing with everything,

205
00:10:31.541 --> 00:10:34.166
it means choosing peace

206
00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:37.666
over proving

207
00:10:37.666 --> 00:10:40.333
a point.

208
00:10:40.333 --> 00:10:41.666
You let go

209
00:10:41.666 --> 00:10:45.875
of the need to win every argument,

210
00:10:45.875 --> 00:10:50.083
and instead focus on

211
00:10:50.083 --> 00:10:54.166
what truly matters,

212
00:10:54.166 --> 00:10:58.458
keeping the bond of affection strong.

213
00:10:58.458 --> 00:11:04.708
When one person in the
family practises forbearance,

214
00:11:04.708 --> 00:11:07.208
it sets the tone

215
00:11:07.208 --> 00:11:10.041
for the whole household.

216
00:11:10.041 --> 00:11:14.000
Less blame and more forgiveness.

217
00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.625
Less tension and more cooperation.

218
00:11:17.625 --> 00:11:22.500
So the next time someone disturbs you,

219
00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.791
pause, smile,

220
00:11:25.791 --> 00:11:28.500
and choose forbearance.

221
00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.458
That one small act can protect

222
00:11:31.458 --> 00:11:36.375
years of love and trust.

223
00:11:41.208 --> 00:11:44.791
If you wish to grow steadily

224
00:11:44.791 --> 00:11:48.416
in professional life,

225
00:11:48.416 --> 00:11:52.708
which two qualities will take you far?

226
00:11:52.708 --> 00:11:56.708
Humility and steadfastness.

227
00:11:56.708 --> 00:11:59.666
Humility helps you keep the door

228
00:11:59.666 --> 00:12:03.333
of the mind open for learning.

229
00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:06.791
It reminds you that however

230
00:12:06.791 --> 00:12:09.208
much you know,

231
00:12:09.208 --> 00:12:11.833
there is always

232
00:12:11.833 --> 00:12:15.291
more to understand.

233
00:12:15.291 --> 00:12:19.083
You do not need to show

234
00:12:19.083 --> 00:12:22.166
that you have all the answers.

235
00:12:22.166 --> 00:12:24.875
When you are humble,

236
00:12:24.875 --> 00:12:25.833
you welcome

237
00:12:25.833 --> 00:12:29.916
feedback,

238
00:12:29.916 --> 00:12:33.000
accept mistakes,

239
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.416
and build stronger bonds

240
00:12:35.416 --> 00:12:38.041
with your team.

241
00:12:38.041 --> 00:12:40.000
But remember,

242
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.791
humility alone

243
00:12:41.791 --> 00:12:45.833
is not enough.

244
00:12:45.833 --> 00:12:48.708
You also need sthairyam,

245
00:12:48.708 --> 00:12:53.083
steadfastness.

246
00:12:53.083 --> 00:12:58.250
Especially when things get difficult.

247
00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.666
Challenges will come,

248
00:13:00.666 --> 00:13:05.666
missed targets, difficult clients, setbacks.

249
00:13:05.666 --> 00:13:07.041
But if you

250
00:13:07.041 --> 00:13:11.458
stay focused on your purpose

251
00:13:11.458 --> 00:13:15.291
and keep making sincere effort,

252
00:13:15.291 --> 00:13:18.208
you will certainly grow.

253
00:13:18.208 --> 00:13:23.708
So be humble enough to keep learning,

254
00:13:23.708 --> 00:13:25.375
and steadfast enough

255
00:13:25.375 --> 00:13:29.500
to never give up.

256
00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:31.000
This balance

257
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:35.125
keeps your ego in check

258
00:13:35.125 --> 00:13:39.708
and your motivation alive.

259
00:13:39.708 --> 00:13:41.666
And when you

260
00:13:41.666 --> 00:13:45.166
lead with these qualities,

261
00:13:45.166 --> 00:13:48.166
you do not just succeed,

262
00:13:48.166 --> 00:13:50.708
you succeed with meaning.
